# Leaderboard and Moderation

## COA

- Moderators have the right to hold, or even reject, any run they deem contrary to the spirit of the rules, even if the grounds for such a rejection are not explicitly listed in these rules. For example, if a runner submits a run that contains a powerful, perhaps 'boundary pushing', trick that has not been shown to the wider community. If you submit a run, you are agreeing to send the game moderators extra proof upon request. Refusal to comply may result in rejection.

## Discord

- Runners are encouraged, but not required, to have access to the discord server. It is the primary hub of our community and the place we hold formal votes on rule changes.

# Proof

## Video

- Runners must provide video proof for all submissions;
- End the video after the run is completed;
- The run should be complete on video;
- The video must not be private;
- The video must not be temporary (such as Twitch past broadcasts);
- If the video is recorded via the replay, the speed must not exceed x2 at all time;
- The speed of the video at the end/completion of a run must not exceed x1;
- Only include what's useful on the video (such as a 2h video for a 10min run);
- The in-game timer must be on the video;
- PvP games are banned on this site.

## Audio

- There is no restriction concerning the audio.

## HUD

- HUD should be shown at all times if possible, whether the video is recorded live or via replay;
- In certain categories, be aware that if the useful information aren't displayed, the run will be rejected.


# Verification

### Please be aware of these limitations:

- Using In-game time, the "Time" slot must be empty and the "In-game time" must be filled;
- Milliseconds are not mandatory, but filling them in would be preferred;
- You must add the patch on your submission;
- Runs must be done in the public Server (PBE is banned);
- Do not use macros or external programs to remap inputs;
- Practice tool is banned unless specified in the rules; 
- "Game breaking" bugs and glitch (triggering a hotfix or a disable) are banned.

